      "source_text": "When the storm weakened, a technician approached the cabinet while wearing a head-mounted camera and an earpiece. Equipment labels contained model numbers, safety notices, alarm codes, and short repair instructions in several languages The local translation system first checked whether the complete label was visible It rejected frames with a missing edge, heavy glare, severe perspective distortion, or poor sharpness in the upper region Four stable frames were required before a photograph was stored if the target was too close. the earpiece asked the technician to step backward If the label was off centre, a simple left or right instruction was played These cues were deliberately brief so they would not compete with environmental sounds or safety communication",
